A||N||1||TRL46202||Oil pan on a V6....||||1||
Z||000000||TRL46202||03-27-2000||08:43 AM||||How hard is it, or is there a procedure (old post) on how to drop the oil pan on a v6? I need to replace/repair an oil leak at the front corner or under the timing chain housing. Is this a comon leak?<P>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||dogtired||03-27-2000||03:53 PM||||I found it to be quite a task!     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Loosened front motor mount, jacked up motor with screw jack and a 2X6 on the oil pan. Put a short 4X4 on each shock tower and a 2X6 across them and chained the motor to it. Removed jack and front motor mount pushed exhaust (very hard to do) out of the way (may be easier to remove it?) then was able to drop the pan, think I may have removed the starter also? You will need a deep 10mm socket for the 2 nuts, the rest are just 10mm bolts.<BR>Thats all I can remember? It has been awhile  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Good luck.||||reg||6
